Note that the Miller-Rabin test is a probabilistic algorithm, so it may return false positives (i.e., a composite number being classified as prime) with a very small probability. Increasing the number of rounds `k` in the `isPrime` function will improve the accuracy of the test but will also increase the computation time."}]

