```go
func Fibfib(n int) int {
	if n < 3 {
        return n - 1
    }

    fibfib := make([]int, n + 1)
    fibfib[0] = 0
    fibfib[1] = 0
    fibfib[2] = 1

    for i := 3; i <= n; i++ {
        fibfib[i] = fibfib[i - 1] + fibfib[i - 2] + fibfib[i - 3]
    }

    return fibfib[n]
}
```

Please keep the following in mind when indexing into arrays and slices in Go: they are 0-indexed. So, for example, the 5th element (not considering 0 index) in our program's output would be `Fibfib(4)` because `Fibfib(0)` is considered to be the 1st element in the sequence. 

