Here is a solution in Go:

```go
func Solve(s string) string {  
    // vowels array
    vowels := []rune{'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}

    // convert input string to rune array for manipulation
    chars := []rune(s) 

    // traverse the rune array   
    for i := 0; i < len(chars); i++ {
        isVowel := false
        isChar := Unicode.IsLetter(chars[i])

        // check if char is vowel
        if isChar {
            for _, v := range vowels {
                if chars[i] == v || chars[i] == unicode.ToUpper(v) {
                    isVowel = true
                    break
                }
            }
        }

        // if vowel then convert to uppercase
        // if consonant then convert to lowercase
        if isVowel {
            chars[i] = unicode.ToUpper(chars[i])
        } else if isChar {
            chars[i] = unicode.ToLower(chars[i])
        }
    }

    // convert the rune array back to string
    return string(chars)
} 
```

This code iterates over the string character by character, and checks if it a vowel or consonant and performs the necessary changes. If the character is a non-alphabetic character, it will remain as it is. If the string doesn't contain any alphabetic characters, they will be removed. This final, modified string is then returned."}]

