```Go
func MatchParens(lst []string) string {
    totalOpen, totalClose := 0, 0

    for _, str := range lst {
        open, close := 0, 0
        for _, char := range str {
            if char == '(' {
                open++
                totalOpen++
            } else if char == ')' {
                close++
                totalClose++
            }
        }
        if close > open {
            return "No"
        }
    }
    if totalOpen != totalClose {
        return "No"
    }
    return "Yes"
}
```

This function works by iterating over each character in each string. When it encounters an open parenthesis, it increments open and totalOpen. When it encounters a closed parenthesis, it increments close and totalClose.

If at any point it sees that close is greater than open, it knows that no further concatenations can balance the string, so it immediately returns "No".

Finally, after checking all characters in all strings, it checks if totalOpen and totalClose are equal. If they are not, it returns "No", as there must be an unmatched parenthesis somewhere. If they are equal, it returns "Yes", as all parentheses must be matched."}]

