The series formula to calculate PI is as follows:

PI = 4 * (1 - (1/3) + (1/5) - (1/7) + (1/9) - (1/11) + ... )

However, it requires many iterations to get an accurate value for PI because it converges slowly.

Here's how you can implement it in C#:

```c#
public static double CalculatePi(int terms)
{
    double sum = 0.0;
    int sign = 1;

    for (int i = 0; i < terms; i++)
    {
        var term = sign/(2.0 * i + 1.0);
        sum += term;
        sign *= -1;
    }

    return 4.0 * sum;
}
```

Just call the following code:

